-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

WHY SWAP DATA instead of moving pointers?

  Moving pointers to insert at beginning needs the LAST node
  to update its next — which means full traversal O(N)

  Swap trick avoids traversal entirely:
    insert temp right after head  →  O(1)
    swap head.data and temp.data  →  O(1)
    head pointer stays the same   →  no need to find last node

  Total time: O(1)  ✅

